  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trinational Response for a Dignified, Peaceful and Inclusive Human Mobility in the North of Central America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is implemented by the International Organization for Migration in partnership with the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees and the United Nations Development Programme in Honduras. It promotes a comprehensive approach to human mobility in the North of Central America countries, as well such as to the challenges for peace that migration can pose for Honduras, Guatemala and El Salvador. This is accomplished through increased coordination between the governments and improving the approach to displacement, irregular migration, protection and sustainable reintegration of people who are part of mixed movements in favor of development and social cohesion. In doing so, this project works to improve capacities of national institutions and civil society to attend to the aforementioned concerns and to have effective protection and sustainable reintegration mechanisms implemented in the prioritized municipalities.</narrative>
  </description>
